text_fidelity_a:
A combinatorial interpretation for the identity Sum_{k=0}^{n}
  binom{n}{k} Sum_{j=0}^{k} binom{k}{j}^{3}= Sum_{k=0}^{n}
  binom{n}{k}^{2}binom{2k}{k}   The title identity appeared as Problem 75-4, proposed by P. Barrucand, in
Siam Review in 1975. The published solution equated constant terms in a
suitable polynomial identity. Here we give a combinatorial interpretation in
terms of card deals.

